Third-party software

The source distribution installs its dependencies with pip and bundles none of them.
The Windows executable (Shoji-*-windows-x64.zip) bundles them; their full license and
NOTICE texts are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt inside that archive. Main components:

  mitmproxy  - MIT License            https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy
  dnslib     - BSD 2-Clause License   https://github.com/paulc/dnslib
  Flask      - BSD 3-Clause License   https://github.com/pallets/flask
  pystray    - LGPL-3.0 (Windows build: shipped as unmodified, replaceable .py files)
  ldap3      - LGPL-3.0 (dependency of mitmproxy; shipped as unmodified, replaceable .py files)
  Pillow     - MIT-CMU (HPND)
  certifi    - MPL-2.0 (unmodified; source at https://github.com/certifi/python-certifi)
  PyInstaller bootloader - GPL-2.0 with an exception permitting distribution of the bundled program

mitmproxy's terminal UI (urwid) and transparent-mode driver (WinDivert/pydivert) are not used
and are excluded from the executable.

Filter lists (downloaded at runtime from their maintainers, not bundled):

  EasyList / EasyPrivacy        https://easylist.to/          (GPLv3 / CC BY-SA 3.0)
  AdGuard filters               https://github.com/AdguardTeam (GPLv3)
  uBlock Origin filters         https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uAssets (GPLv3)
  AdGuard DNS filter            https://github.com/AdguardTeam/AdGuardSDNSFilter (GPLv3)
  Peter Lowe's Ad and tracking server list   https://pgl.yoyo.org/adservers/

Each list remains under its own license and is used unmodified. Shoji's own
built-in rules (rules/builtin_*.txt) are original to this project.
